error[E0277]: `sqlx::Sqlite` has no row locks, so a table on it cannot use the row lock form
  --> tests/ui/sqlite_row_lock.rs:14:47
   |
14 |     let _ = InboxQueue::<Locked>::new("jobs").subscribe(connected).await;
   |                                               ^^^^^^^^^ a table without `locked_until` or `advisory_lock` takes rows by row lock
   |
   = help: the trait `RowLocks` is not implemented for `sqlx::Sqlite`
   = note: declare `#[field(locked_until)]` (the lease form) or `#[inbox(advisory_lock = "..")]` (the advisory lock form) on the struct
help: the trait `SubscriptionSource<ConnectedSqlxBroker<DB>>` is conditionally implemented for `InboxQueue<Row>`
  --> src/inbox/queue.rs
   |
   | / impl<DB, Row> SubscriptionSource<ConnectedSqlxBroker<DB>> for InboxQueue<Row>
   | | where
   | |     DB: QueueDatabase,
   | |     Row: InboxRow + Events<DB> + PayloadRow,
   | |     Row::Form: FormOn<DB>,
   | |________________----------^
   |                  |
   |                  unsatisfied requirement introduced here: `<Locked as InboxRow>::Form: ruststream_sqlx::__private::FormOn<sqlx::Sqlite>`
   = note: required for `ruststream_sqlx::__private::RowLockForm` to implement `ruststream_sqlx::__private::FormOn<sqlx::Sqlite>`
   = note: required for `InboxQueue<Locked>` to implement `SubscriptionSource<ConnectedSqlxBroker<sqlx::Sqlite>>`

